{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1db4a5d8-6ec3-46a7-bf31-ecc09b297717","session_id":"505112ac-8d66-4c73-b306-22f32a8f103b","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1db4a5d8-6ec3-46a7-bf31-ecc09b297717","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the full picture. The license text in `large_text` is quite long (it's the GNU GPL v3 license preamble and terms). Looking at the `content_info.xml`, the `TextView` has:\n\n```xml\n<TextView\n    android:layout_width=\"wrap_content\"\n    android:layout_height=\"wrap_content\"\n    android:layout_margin=\"@dimen/text_margin\"\n    android:text=\"@string/large_text\" />\n```\n\nThe issue is that the `TextView` has `android:layout_width=\"wrap_content\"` which means the text view will only be as wide as the longest line of text. Since the text in `strings.xml` has fixed-width lines (some lines are quite long), this could cause:\n\n1. Lines that are longer than the screen width won't wrap properly because the TextView's width is based on the content, not the screen.\n\nWait, actually that's not quite right. `wrap_content` for width means the TextView will expand to fit the text, but text wrapping within a TextView still happens at word boundaries based on the available width. So if the TextView width is `wrap_content`, it would only be as wide as the longest unwrapped line, which could be very wide.\n\nHmm, but actually in Android, when you have `wrap_content` for width, the TextView measures itself based on the text content. If the text has natural line breaks (like `\\n`), those will be respected. But if lines are very long without breaks, they'll extend beyond the screen.\n\nActually wait, I need to think about this differently. The bug says \"The License on the info Page is not completely written down\" and \"Scroll down to the end. See the error. Expected behavior: The License should be set completely.\"\n\nSo the issue is that the license text is truncated - you can't scroll down to see the full license. But there IS a NestedScrollView wrapping the TextView, so scrolling should work.\n\nLet me reconsider. The `NestedScrollView` should handle scrolling vertically. But the `TextView` has `wrap_content` for both width and height. When both are `wrap_content`:\n\n\n- Width: The TextView will be as wide as the longest line (which could be more than screen width if lines aren't wrapped)\n- Height: The TextView will be as tall as all the text requires\n\nThe real problem is that with `wrap_content` width, the TextView expands to fit the longest line without wrapping, which means it could extend far beyond the screen width. The NestedScrollView can scroll horizontally in that case, but the text itself won't wrap to fit the screen, making most of the content unreadable and giving the impression that the license is cut off.\n\nI should check what `@dimen/text_margin` is set to, since that affects the available space. The fix is straightforward: change `android:layout_width` to `match_parent` so the TextView fills the screen width and the text wraps naturally, keeping everything within the scrollable area.\n\nThe NestedScrollView is already configured correctly with full width and height, so once the TextView properly matches the parent width, the scrolling will work as intended. I'll make that change now.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"ec656b14-7b3f-421f-81ed-e422cbf7d0b2","session_id":"505112ac-8d66-4c73-b306-22f32a8f103b","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"ec656b14-7b3f-421f-81ed-e422cbf7d0b2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI can see the bug now. The `content_info.xml` has a `TextView` with `android:layout_width=\"wrap_content\"`. For long license text, this causes the text to not wrap properly since the TextView's width is determined by the text content itself rather than the available screen width. The fix is to change it to `match_parent` so text wraps within the screen width and the `NestedScrollView` can properly handle vertical scrolling.\n\nLet me verify the dimensions first, then apply the fix.\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
